{"id":"mahabharata-12-312","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":312,"title":"द्वादशाधिकत्रिशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 312 · Shuka goes to Mithila","summary":{"en":"Shuka, thinking of liberation, asks his father for the way, and Vyasa sends him to Janaka, king of Mithila, to learn. Shuka travels through the air as if walking, crosses the lands, and at last spends a night in the house of the king.","kn":"ಮೋಕ್ಷ ಚಿಂತಿಸುವ ಶುಕ ತಂದೆಯ ಬಳಿ ದಾರಿ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ, ವ್ಯಾಸ ಕಲಿಯಲು ಮಿಥಿಲೆಯ ಜನಕನ ಬಳಿ ಕಳುಹಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಶುಕ ಆಕಾಶದಲ್ಲಿ ನಡೆದಂತೆ ಸಂಚರಿಸಿ ಪ್ರದೇಶಗಳನ್ನು ದಾಟಿ ಕೊನೆಗೆ ರಾಜನ ಮನೆಯಲ್ಲಿ ರಾತ್ರಿ ಕಳೆಯುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"मोक्ष का चिन्तन करते शुक पिता से मार्ग पूछते हैं और व्यास उन्हें सीखने के लिए मिथिला के राजा जनक के पास भेजते हैं। शुक आकाश में चलते हुए देशों को पार करते हैं और अन्त में राजा के घर रात बिताते हैं।","te":"మోక్ష చింతనలో ఉన్న శుకుడు తండ్రిని మార్గం అడుగుతాడు, వ్యాసుడు నేర్చుకోవడానికి మిథిలా రాజు జనకుని వద్దకు పంపుతాడు. శుకుడు ఆకాశంలో నడిచినట్లు సంచరించి ప్రాంతాలను దాటి చివరకు రాజు ఇంట్లో రాత్రి గడుపుతాడు.","ta":"விடுதலையை எண்ணும் சுகர் தந்தையிடம் வழி கேட்க, வியாசர் கற்பதற்காக மிதிலை மன்னன் ஜனகனிடம் அனுப்புகிறார். சுகர் வானில் நடப்பது போல் பயணித்து நாடுகளைக் கடந்து இறுதியில் மன்னனின் இல்லத்தில் இரவு தங்குகிறார்.","ml":"മോക്ഷം ചിന്തിച്ച ശുകൻ അതിന്റെ വഴി പിതാവിനോട് ചോദിക്കുന്നു; പഠിക്കാൻ വ്യാസൻ അദ്ദേഹത്തെ മിഥിലയിലെ രാജാവായ ജനകന്റെ അടുത്തേക്ക് അയയ്ക്കുന്നു. നടക്കുന്നതുപോലെ ശുകൻ ആകാശത്തിലൂടെ സഞ്ചരിച്ച് ദേശങ്ങൾ കടക്കുന്നു, ഒടുവിൽ രാജാവിന്റെ വീട്ടിൽ ഒരു രാത്രി കഴിയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.312; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"मोक्षधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Mokshadharma Parva (Duties for liberation)","verses":[{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"स मोक्षमनुचिन्त्यैव शुकः पितरमभ्यगात् ।\nप्राहाभिवाद्य च गुरुं श्रेयोर्थी विनयान्वितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reflecting on liberation, Shuka went to his father, greeted his teacher, and humbly spoke, eager for the highest good."}},{"n":2,"text":"मोक्षधर्मेषु कुशलो भगवान्प्रब्रवीतु मे ।\nयथा मे मनसः शान्तिः परमा संभवेत्प्रभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Master, you are skilled in the teachings on liberation; tell me, lord, how my mind may find the supreme peace.\""}},{"n":3,"text":"श्रुत्वा पुत्रस्य वचनं परमर्षिरुवाच तम् ।\nअधीष्व पुत्र मोक्षं वै धर्मांश्च विविधानपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing his son's words, the great sage replied: \"Study, my son, liberation and the many kinds of dharma.\""}},{"n":4,"text":"पितुर्नियोगाज्जग्राह शुको ब्रह्मविदां वरः ।\nयोगशास्त्रं च निखिलं कापिलं चैव भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"At his father's bidding Shuka, best of the knowers of Brahman, mastered all of yoga teaching and the Kapila system as well, Bharata."}},{"n":5,"text":"स तं ब्राह्म्या श्रिया युक्तं ब्रह्मतुल्यपराक्रमम् ।\nमेने पुत्रं यदा व्यासो मोक्षविद्याविशारदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Vyasa saw his son, radiant with the splendor of Brahman, matching Brahman in vigor and expert in the science of liberation,"}},{"n":6,"text":"उवाच गच्छेति तदा जनकं मिथिलेश्वरम् ।\nस ते वक्ष्यति मोक्षार्थं निखिलेन विशेषतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"he told him: \"Go to Janaka, lord of Mithila; he will explain liberation to you fully and in particular.\""}},{"n":7,"text":"पितुर्नियोगादगमन्मैथिलं जनकं नृपम् ।\nप्रष्टुं धर्मस्य निष्ठां वै मोक्षस्य च परायणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"On his father's order he went to King Janaka of Mithila, to ask about the final basis of dharma and the highest refuge of liberation."}},{"n":8,"text":"उक्तश्च मानुषेण त्वं पथा गच्छेत्यविस्मितः ।\nन प्रभावेण गन्तव्यमन्तरिक्षचरेण वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vyasa said: \"Go as a human does, without conceit, not by your power, not through the sky."}},{"n":9,"text":"आर्जवेणैव गन्तव्यं न सुखान्वेषिणा पथा ।\nनान्वेष्टव्या विशेषास्तु विशेषा हि प्रसङ्गिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Go with simplicity, not by an easy road; do not seek distinctions, for distinctions bind to attachment."}},{"n":10,"text":"अहंकारो न कर्तव्यो याज्ये तस्मिन्नराधिपे ।\nस्थातव्यं च वशे तस्य स ते छेत्स्यति संशयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Show no arrogance toward that king, for whom I perform sacrifices; stay under his direction, and he will cut your doubt."}},{"n":11,"text":"स धर्मकुशलो राजा मोक्षशास्त्रविशारदः ।\nयाज्यो मम स यद्ब्रूयात्तत्कार्यमविशङ्कया ॥","meaning":{"en":"That king is skilled in dharma and expert in the science of liberation; whatever he says, he who is my patron, do without hesitation.\""}},{"n":12,"text":"एवमुक्तः स धर्मात्मा जगाम मिथिलां मुनिः ।\nपद्भ्यां शक्तोऽन्तरिक्षेण क्रान्तुं भूमिं ससागराम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So instructed, the righteous sage went toward Mithila, though he was able to cross the earth with its oceans on foot or through the sky."}},{"n":13,"text":"स गिरींश्चाप्यतिक्रम्य नदीस्तीर्त्वा सरांसि च ।\nबहुव्यालमृगाकीर्णा विविधाश्चाटवीस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"He crossed mountains, forded rivers and lakes, and passed through varied forests full of wild beasts and predators."}},{"n":14,"text":"मेरोर्हरेश्च द्वे वर्षे वर्षं हैमवतं तथा ।\nक्रमेणैव व्यतिक्रम्य भारतं वर्षमासदत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In order he passed the two regions of Meru and Hari and the region Haimavata, and reached the land of Bharata."}},{"n":15,"text":"स देशान्विविधान्पश्यंश्चीनहूणनिषेवितान् ।\nआर्यावर्तमिमं देशमाजगाम महामुनिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing many lands inhabited by Chinas and Hunas, the great sage came to this country of Aryavarta."}},{"n":16,"text":"पितुर्वचनमाज्ञाय तमेवार्थं विचिन्तयन् ।\nअध्वानं सोऽतिचक्राम खेऽचरः खे चरन्निव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Keeping his father's words in mind and pondering only that purpose, he covered the road, moving over the ground as if moving through the sky."}},{"n":17,"text":"पत्तनानि च रम्याणि स्फीतानि नगराणि च ।\nरत्नानि च विचित्राणि शुकः पश्यन्न पश्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shuka saw lovely towns, prosperous cities, and wondrous jewels, yet saw none of them."}},{"n":18,"text":"उद्यानानि च रम्याणि तथैवायतनानि च ।\nपुण्यानि चैव तीर्थानि सोऽतिक्रम्य तथाध्वनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having passed beautiful gardens, shrines, and holy bathing places along the way,"}},{"n":19,"text":"सोऽचिरेणैव कालेन विदेहानाससाद ह ।\nरक्षितान्धर्मराजेन जनकेन महात्मना ॥","meaning":{"en":"in no long time he reached the Videhas, protected by the great and righteous King Janaka."}},{"n":20,"text":"तत्र ग्रामान्बहून्पश्यन्बह्वन्नरसभोजनान् ।\nपल्लीघोषान्समृद्धांश्च बहुगोकुलसंकुलान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There he saw many villages with abundant food, prosperous herdsmen's settlements crowded with herds of cattle,"}},{"n":21,"text":"स्फीतांश्च शालियवसैर्हंससारससेवितान् ।\nपद्मिनीभिश्च शतशः श्रीमतीभिरलंकृतान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"rich with rice and barley, visited by swans and cranes, and adorned with hundreds of lovely lotus ponds."}},{"n":22,"text":"स विदेहानतिक्रम्य समृद्धजनसेवितान् ।\nमिथिलोपवनं रम्यमाससाद महर्द्धिमत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Passing beyond the Videhas, who were served by prosperous people, he reached the beautiful and wealthy groves of Mithila."}},{"n":23,"text":"हस्त्यश्वरथसंकीर्णं नरनारीसमाकुलम् ।\nपश्यन्नपश्यन्निव तत्समतिक्रामदच्युतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Crowded with elephants, horses, and chariots and thronged with men and women, he passed it, the unshaken one, seeing yet not seeing."}},{"n":24,"text":"मनसा तं वहन्भारं तमेवार्थं विचिन्तयन् ।\nआत्मारामः प्रसन्नात्मा मिथिलामाससाद ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Carrying that burden in his mind and pondering that one aim, content in the Self and serene, he arrived at Mithila."}},{"n":25,"text":"तस्या द्वारं समासाद्य द्वारपालैर्निवारितः ।\nस्थितो ध्यानपरो मुक्तो विदितः प्रविवेश ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"At its gate the gatekeepers stopped him; he stood absorbed in meditation, free of attachment, and once recognized he entered."}},{"n":26,"text":"स राजमार्गमासाद्य समृद्धजनसंकुलम् ।\nपार्थिवक्षयमासाद्य निःशङ्कः प्रविवेश ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"He reached the royal road crowded with prosperous people and, reaching the king's residence, entered without fear."}},{"n":27,"text":"तत्रापि द्वारपालास्तमुग्रवाचो न्यषेधयन् ।\nतथैव च शुकस्तत्र निर्मन्युः समतिष्ठत ॥","meaning":{"en":"There too harsh-voiced gatekeepers barred him, and again Shuka stood there without anger."}},{"n":28,"text":"न चातपाध्वसंतप्तः क्षुत्पिपासाश्रमान्वितः ।\nप्रताम्यति ग्लायति वा नापैति च तथातपात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Not scorched by the sun on the road nor weary with hunger, thirst, or fatigue, he neither wilted nor tired, nor did he leave the heat."}},{"n":29,"text":"तेषां तु द्वारपालानामेकः शोकसमन्वितः ।\nमध्यंगतमिवादित्यं दृष्ट्वा शुकमवस्थितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One of those gatekeepers, moved with feeling, saw Shuka standing like the sun at midday."}},{"n":30,"text":"पूजयित्वा यथान्यायमभिवाद्य कृताञ्जलिः ।\nप्रावेशयत्ततः कक्ष्यां द्वितीयां राजवेश्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He honored him properly, greeted him with folded hands, and led him into the second court of the royal palace."}},{"n":31,"text":"तत्रासीनः शुकस्तात मोक्षमेवानुचिन्तयन् ।\nछायायामातपे चैव समदर्शी महाद्युतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seated there, dear Bharata, the greatly radiant Shuka contemplated only liberation, equal-minded in shade and in sun."}},{"n":32,"text":"तं मुहूर्तादिवागम्य राज्ञो मन्त्री कृताञ्जलिः ।\nप्रावेशयत्ततः कक्ष्यां तृतीयां राजवेश्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"After a moment the king's minister came with folded hands and led him into the third court of the palace."}},{"n":33,"text":"तत्रान्तःपुरसंबद्धं महच्चैत्ररथोपमम् ।\nसुविभक्तजलाक्रीडं रम्यं पुष्पितपादपम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There was a great garden joined to the women's quarters, like Chaitraratha, with well-laid pleasure pools and flowering trees."}},{"n":34,"text":"तद्दर्शयित्वा स शुकं मन्त्री काननमुत्तमम् ।\nअर्हमासनमादिश्य निश्चक्राम ततः पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Showing Shuka that excellent grove, the minister assigned him a fitting seat and then went out again."}},{"n":35,"text":"तं चारुवेषाः सुश्रोण्यस्तरुण्यः प्रियदर्शनाः ।\nसूक्ष्मरक्ताम्बरधरास्तप्तकाञ्चनभूषणाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lovely young women, fair of hip and pleasing to see, wearing fine red garments and ornaments of refined gold,"}},{"n":36,"text":"संलापोल्लापकुशला नृत्तगीतविशारदाः ।\nस्मितपूर्वाभिभाषिण्यो रूपेणाप्सरसां समाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"skilled in talk and banter, expert in dance and song, speaking with a smile first, equal to apsaras in beauty,"}},{"n":37,"text":"कामोपचारकुशला भावज्ञाः सर्वकोविदाः ।\nपरं पञ्चाशतो नार्यो वारमुख्याः समाद्रवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"skilled in arts of love, reading moods, knowing everything, more than fifty courtesans, ran up to him."}},{"n":38,"text":"पाद्यादीनि प्रतिग्राह्य पूजया परयार्च्य च ।\nदेशकालोपपन्नेन साध्वन्नेनाप्यतर्पयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They received him with water for his feet and other rites, honored him greatly, and fed him with good food suited to place and time."}},{"n":39,"text":"तस्य भुक्तवतस्तात तदन्तःपुरकाननम् ।\nसुरम्यं दर्शयामासुरेकैकश्येन भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"When he had eaten, dear Bharata, they showed him one by one the lovely garden of the women's quarters."}},{"n":40,"text":"क्रीडन्त्यश्च हसन्त्यश्च गायन्त्यश्चैव ताः शुकम् ।\nउदारसत्त्वं सत्त्वज्ञाः सर्वाः पर्यचरंस्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Playing, laughing, and singing, they all attended on Shuka, the noble-souled, knowing well the nature of beings."}},{"n":41,"text":"आरणेयस्तु शुद्धात्मा त्रिसंदेहस्त्रिकर्मकृत् ।\nवश्येन्द्रियो जितक्रोधो न हृष्यति न कुप्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"But the son of Arani, pure in self, free from the three doubts and doing the three acts, with senses under control and anger conquered, felt neither joy nor irritation."}},{"n":42,"text":"तस्मै शय्यासनं दिव्यं वरार्हं रत्नभूषितम् ।\nस्पर्ध्यास्तरणसंस्तीर्णं ददुस्ताः परमस्त्रियः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those excellent women gave him a divine bed and seat, worthy of the finest, decked with jewels and spread with enviable coverings."}},{"n":43,"text":"पादशौचं तु कृत्वैव शुकः संध्यामुपास्य च ।\nनिषसादासने पुण्ये तमेवार्थं विचिन्तयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"After washing his feet and performing the twilight worship, Shuka sat on the pure seat, pondering only that same aim."}},{"n":44,"text":"पूर्वरात्रे तु तत्रासौ भूत्वा ध्यानपरायणः ।\nमध्यरात्रे यथान्यायं निद्रामाहारयत्प्रभुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the first part of the night he remained absorbed in meditation, and at midnight the lord took sleep as is proper."}},{"n":45,"text":"ततो मुहूर्तादुत्थाय कृत्वा शौचमनन्तरम् ।\nस्त्रीभिः परिवृतो धीमान्ध्यानमेवान्वपद्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then rising after a moment and finishing his purification, surrounded by the women, the wise one took up meditation again."}},{"n":46,"text":"अनेन विधिना कार्ष्णिस्तदहःशेषमच्युतः ।\nतां च रात्रिं नृपकुले वर्तयामास भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"In this manner, Bharata, Krishna's son, unshaken, passed the rest of that day and that night in the king's household."}}]}]}